WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.924 --> 00:00:12.107
I at Josh.

2
00:00:12.807 --> 00:00:15.388
Bunch was gone—really gone?

3
00:00:17.869 --> 00:00:20.569
Josh, Jenny, Molly, and I hurried outside.

4
00:00:21.230 --> 00:00:22.430
Caswell followed us.

5
00:00:22.450 --> 00:00:26.671
"I don't understand what's wrong," said Molly.

6
00:00:26.691 --> 00:00:29.892
"Wasn't Bunch supposed to disappear?"

7
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:34.842
"Yes, but Bunch truly disappeared," Josh told her.

8
00:00:34.862 --> 00:00:37.723
"Even my dad doesn't know where he is.

9
00:00:38.043 --> 00:00:39.323
We've got to find him fast."

10
00:00:40.484 --> 00:00:41.904
Jenny was about to cry.

11
00:00:41.924 --> 00:00:44.045
"Poor Bunch!

12
00:00:44.065 --> 00:00:46.026
He could be lost!"

13
00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:50.068
"I wonder how he got out of the box," I said.

14
00:00:50.088 --> 00:00:53.049
"I didn't mean to do it!"

15
00:00:53.409 --> 00:00:54.409
cried Caswell.

16
00:00:56.010 --> 00:00:57.531
We all stared at him.

17
00:00:57.551 --> 00:01:00.392
"Caswell!" said Molly.

18
00:01:01.184 --> 00:01:02.184
"What did you do?"

19
00:01:02.204 --> 00:01:08.786
"I opened the box when I was under the table," said Caswell, hanging his head.

20
00:01:08.806 --> 00:01:12.868
"I wanted to see how Bunch disappeared."

21
00:01:12.888 --> 00:01:17.269
"So that's how Bunch escaped," I said.

22
00:01:17.289 --> 00:01:19.530
"But where is he now?"

23
00:01:21.090 --> 00:01:22.611
Caswell looked worried.

24
00:01:22.631 --> 00:01:26.492
"I hope Bunch doesn't get stranded in the mountains."

25
00:01:29.984 --> 00:01:34.187
"Too bad he didn't have any rainbow trail pellets, Iggy," said Molly.

26
00:01:34.207 --> 00:01:37.529
"Then we could follow his pellet trail."

27
00:01:38.610 --> 00:01:39.811
I glanced at the ground.

28
00:01:40.792 --> 00:01:44.734
Luckily, most of the pellets that had spilled out earlier were still there.

29
00:01:45.715 --> 00:01:47.496
Then I noticed something.

30
00:01:47.516 --> 00:01:49.377
"Look, guys!"

31
00:01:49.818 --> 00:01:50.218
I said.

32
00:01:50.238 --> 00:01:53.240
"Only the red pellets are left."

33
00:01:53.260 --> 00:01:58.564
"What happened to all the other colors?"

34
00:01:59.160 --> 00:01:59.901
asked Molly.

35
00:01:59.921 --> 00:02:02.302
"Bunch ate them!"

36
00:02:02.682 --> 00:02:03.202
I cried.

37
00:02:03.222 --> 00:02:06.044
"Except for all the red ones.

38
00:02:06.424 --> 00:02:07.725
Bunch doesn't like red.

39
00:02:08.165 --> 00:02:14.028
Remember?" "Maybe the trail of red pellets will lead to Bunch!"

40
00:02:14.569 --> 00:02:15.249
said Jenny.

41
00:02:15.269 --> 00:02:17.350
"I'll go tell my dad!"

42
00:02:17.690 --> 00:02:18.351
said Josh.

43
00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:20.852
"Wait!" I said.

44
00:02:20.872 --> 00:02:22.693
"I have an idea.

45
00:02:23.073 --> 00:02:24.954
The audience can help look for Bunch.

46
00:02:25.435 --> 00:02:27.836
Finding Bunch can be part of the magic trick."

47
00:02:28.844 --> 00:02:31.566
"Awesome idea, Iggy," said Josh.

48
00:02:33.687 --> 00:02:34.588
Inside, Mr.

49
00:02:34.688 --> 00:02:36.850
Chen was finishing his string trick.

50
00:02:40.372 --> 00:02:42.594
Josh rushed up and whispered to him.

51
00:02:43.954 --> 00:02:46.776
Mr. Chen nodded and then turned back to the crowd.

52
00:02:46.796 --> 00:02:51.760
"We will now return to the vanishing dog trick," he announced.

53
00:02:51.780 --> 00:02:54.982
"For this, I have a special surprise.

54
00:02:55.442 --> 00:02:57.544
Everyone, please follow me outside."

55
00:02:58.400 --> 00:02:59.861
The audience followed Mr.

56
00:02:59.921 --> 00:03:00.801
Chen outside.

57
00:03:03.722 --> 00:03:06.163
Mr. Scary trailed along, frowning.

58
00:03:06.183 --> 00:03:11.445
"This is a very unusual trick," he muttered.

59
00:03:11.465 --> 00:03:14.887
"Are you absolutely sure it will work?"

60
00:03:16.768 --> 00:03:18.308
I could see a little doubt in Mr.

61
00:03:18.368 --> 00:03:20.969
Chen's eyes too, but he nodded at Mr.

62
00:03:21.029 --> 00:03:25.791
Scary. "Find the trail of red, and it will lead to the dog!"

63
00:03:26.231 --> 00:03:27.352
he called to the audience.

64
00:03:28.436 --> 00:03:30.618
"Now let's all say the magic words."

65
00:03:31.698 --> 00:03:34.500
"Abracadabra, click and clack.

66
00:03:34.740 --> 00:03:37.542
Bring that little dog right back!"

67
00:03:37.902 --> 00:03:38.743
said the audience.

68
00:03:44.386 --> 00:03:47.568
Everyone followed the trail of red pellets up to the tower.

69
00:03:47.588 --> 00:03:50.790
"I see him!

70
00:03:51.270 --> 00:03:52.611
There's the doggie!"

71
00:03:53.071 --> 00:03:53.932
cried Brandy.

72
00:03:55.000 --> 00:03:59.421
Sure enough, there was Bunch, sitting near the tower, licking his lips.

73
00:04:03.263 --> 00:04:04.223
a great trick!"

74
00:04:04.703 --> 00:04:06.403
cried the lady in the blue hat.

75
00:04:06.423 --> 00:04:11.325
"Hmm that was quite a trick," said Mr.

76
00:04:11.405 --> 00:04:14.086
Scary. "How did you do it?"

77
00:04:14.606 --> 00:04:15.446
he asked Mr.

78
00:04:15.506 --> 00:04:17.047
Chen. Mr.

79
00:04:17.067 --> 00:04:17.887
Chen smiled.

80
00:04:17.907 --> 00:04:21.148
"A magician never reveals his secrets."

81
00:04:23.876 --> 00:04:28.819
After that everyone trooped back down to the Lake Lounge for lemonade and cookies.

82
00:04:28.839 --> 00:04:34.242
"Iggy's special pellet invention saved the day," said Josh.

83
00:04:34.262 --> 00:04:37.824
"It certainly did," said Mr.

84
00:04:37.904 --> 00:04:41.346
Chen. "That was a very fine invention, Iggy."

85
00:04:41.366 --> 00:04:47.049
"But, Caswell," said Molly, "don't ever interfere with Mr.

86
00:04:47.109 --> 00:04:48.730
Chen's magic show again."

87
00:04:48.750 --> 00:04:54.240
"I won't," promised Caswell, grabbing another cookie.

88
00:04:54.260 --> 00:04:56.861
"I wonder why Mr.

89
00:04:56.921 --> 00:04:59.102
Scary keeps staring at my dad?"

90
00:04:59.502 --> 00:05:01.062
said Josh in a low voice.

91
00:05:01.082 --> 00:05:05.183
"He looks like he has something up his sleeve," I said.

92
00:05:05.203 --> 00:05:08.404
"Does he have a gold coin up his sleeve?"

93
00:05:08.764 --> 00:05:09.725
asked Caswell.

94
00:05:09.745 --> 00:05:12.505
"Is he going to do a magic trick?"

95
00:05:12.525 --> 00:05:15.606
"No, Caswell," Molly said.

96
00:05:15.626 --> 00:05:17.747
"Iggy just means that Mr.

97
00:05:17.807 --> 00:05:19.507
Scary is plotting something."

98
00:05:20.588 --> 00:05:22.846
"Maybe it's something good," said Josh.

99
00:05:23.949 --> 00:05:25.031
I didn't say anything.

100
00:05:25.693 --> 00:05:27.156
But I was watching Mr.

101
00:05:27.236 --> 00:05:28.279
Scary closely.

102
00:05:28.299 --> 00:05:31.727
And I didn't think he was plotting anything good.
